837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440482 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440480 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440482 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440482 1077 "selection" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440482 1078 #edb/ref 17592186440478 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440482 1079 #uuid "ad94b206-3ccb-5817-8ec1-05230e22359f" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440483 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440472 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440483 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440474 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440483 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440477 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440483 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440479 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440483 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440481 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440483 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440483 1077 "selection" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440483 1078 #edb/ref 17592186440474 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440483 1079 #uuid "e1483cc5-4c9b-5aca-8098-5a910582cb85" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440484 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440483 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440484 1069 "q-130770" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440484 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440484 1071 "Suppose $Y$ is a $9\\times 9$ matrix and $det(Y)=75.$ The matrix $Z$ is obtained from $Y$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{8}↔{R}_{9}$ and ${R}_{7}:={R}_{7}+\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{2}.$ What is the value of $det(Z)?$" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440484 1072 #uuid "ba8abd45-3c22-5be5-a8a7-0f2c616dbcc7" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440484 1074 "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{8}↔{R}_{9}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{7}:={R}_{7}+\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{2}$ involves adding a multiple of one row to another row,  so it does not change the determinant.\n\nTherefore, we only have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Z) & =-det(Y) \\\\  & =-(75) \\\\  & =-75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440485 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440482 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440485 1069 "q-72744" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440485 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440485 1071 "Suppose $X$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(X)=-3.$ What is the value of $det(7X)?$" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440485 1072 #uuid "fc497788-364d-5c29-8657-a4f1556e2704" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440485 1074 "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot X)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(X).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=7$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(7X) & ={7}^{2}\\cdot det(X) \\\\  & =49\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-147.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440486 1062 #uuid "0b56b3f3-0eed-5dd2-8e0f-81ffa9b89ff3" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440486 1063 #edb/ref 17592186378657 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440487 1058 #edb/ref 17592186440488 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440487 1062 #uuid "1776f775-68f2-5dfe-9a78-5fcd889a28cc" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440487 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265972 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440488 1058 #edb/ref 17592186440486 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440488 1062 #uuid "bc80a516-1dfa-5188-a931-81163ba5b5d8" 13194139534837 17592186045417 true] [17592186440488 1063 #edb/ref 17592186383216 13194